# iTantra Backend API Integration Guide

This document outlines how the mobile frontend communicates with the central C2 (Command & Control) backend. Note that this backend is **only used when internet connectivity is available** (e.g., model downloading, historic backlog sync). Live Walkie-Talkie communication uses the offline P2P transport.

## 1. Environments & Base URLs
| Environment | REST URL | WebSocket URL |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Production Cloud (Render)** | `https://itantra-backend-bwoq.onrender.com` | `wss://itantra-backend-bwoq.onrender.com` |
| **Local Emulator** | `http://10.0.2.2:3000` | `ws://10.0.2.2:3000` |
| **Physical Device (LAN)** | `http://<YOUR_IPV4>:3000` | `ws://<YOUR_IPV4>:3000` |


